Money formatting via toLocaleString with currency options (model assumes Intl-like behavior).
-- script.js --
const rows = mcp.ledger.totals({}).rows;
return rows.map(r => [
  r.amount.toLocaleString(),
  r.amount.toLocaleString("en-US"),
  r.amount.toLocaleString("en-US", {style: "currency", currency: "USD"}),
  r.amount.toLocaleString(undefined, {maximumFractionDigits: 0}),
  r.amount.toLocaleString("de-DE", {minimumFractionDigits: 2}),
]);
-- tools.json --
{
  "ledger.totals": {
    "rows": [
      {
        "amount": 1234567.891
      },
      {
        "amount": -0.5
      },
      {
        "amount": 0
      },
      {
        "amount": 1e+21
      },
      {
        "amount": 12.3456
      }
    ]
  }
}
-- divergence --
Goja reads toLocaleString's first argument as a radix and throws "RangeError: toString() radix argument must be between 2 and 36"; the native engine formats through Intl.NumberFormat as ECMA-402 specifies (English data only: "de-DE" resolves to "en-US"), matching Node/ICU for English locales. Without arguments both return Goja's plain number string.
